ing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T15:20:57Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T16:53:46Z","body":"Looks like there may be a bit of a road bump with adding test cases: the GDScriptTestRunner specifically suppresses the `UNTYPED_DECLARATION` and `INFERRED_DECLARATION` warnings.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/839de3dfd69233476031693114087e5095dd5432/modules/gdscript/tests/gdscript_test_runner.cpp#L149-L164\r\n\r\nGiven the TODO comment there, I don't think there's a way for me to selectively make the `UNTYPED_DECLARATION` warning emit for my particular test.\r\n\r\nIndeed, I tried writing the following test:\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc test():\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nfunc regular_function(_arg):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nfunc vararg_function(..._var_args):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n```\r\nAnd the resultant `.out` file is simply\r\n```\r\nGDTEST_OK\r\n\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5106075470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5120913332","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121839#issuecomment-5120913332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121839","id":5120913332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMTrvtA","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T16:53:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T16:53:36Z","body":"Alright, as part of this PR the test runner system has now been updated to check for comments `# enable UNTYPED_DECLARATION` and `# enable INFERRED_DECLARATION` in each test file. If found, the corresponding warning is temporarily enabled for that file only. With this change in place, the warning test now produces the correct warnings:\r\n```gdscript\r\n# enable UNTYPED_DECLARATION\r\n\r\nfunc test() -> void:\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nfunc regular_function(_arg) -> void:\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nfunc vararg_function(..._var_args) -> void:\r\n    pass\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nGDTEST_OK\r\n~~ WARNING at line 6: (UNTYPED_DECLARATION) Parameter \"_arg\" has no static type.\r\n~~ WARNING at line 9: (UNTYPED_DECLARATION) Parameter \"_var_args\" has no static type.\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5120913332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":n